1
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:26,240
<i>I will never forget the good times</i>
<i>we had together.</i>

2
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,560
<i>And one day,</i>

3
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,240
<i>I'll come find you.</i>

4
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,680
No! Ouch!

5
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,840
But this is our last bit of money.

6
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,800
<i>Tomorrow you might love them.</i>

7
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,920
<i>From feeling indifferent,</i>

8
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,760
<i>it might turn into something special.</i>

9
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,520
<i>From hopelessness,</i>

10
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:50,720
<i>it starts turning into hope.</i>

11
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,760
<i>From pity</i>

12
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,080
<i>and sympathy,</i>

13
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:57,640
<i>it becomes</i>

14
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,080
<i>love.</i>

15
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:02,320
Aunt Eiang said
you don't have many friends.

16
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,400
Don't you get lonely?

17
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,160
Am I being too direct?

18
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,080
No.

19
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,080
Not direct?

20
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,760
I'm not lonely.

21
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,080
I have work. I'm not lonely.

22
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,960
Wow, that's nice.
You're not the type to feel lonely.

23
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,760
I can't do that at all.
I always need people around me.

24
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,640
My parents, my friends.

25
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,240
I always need someone
to talk to, to vent to.

26
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,680
When I'm bored, I call them to gossip.
When I'm tired, I drag them out to eat.

27
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:40,640
Once I feel better, I go back to work.

28
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:43,800
That's good.

29
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,600
But if you find someone
you feel comfortable with,

30
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:53,200
even if things get chaotic,
you'll get used to it eventually.

31
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,440
Fuang.

32
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,160
Yes?

33
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,280
Whoa!

34
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,240
Ugh.

35
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,520
It got all over my pants.

36
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,560
Let's call it a day.

37
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,560
Go home and wash your pants.

38
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,800
Okay.

39
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:49,040
Then where should I come tomorrow?
What time?

40
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,040
No more work tomorrow.

41
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,520
Just finish the report
and submit it. That's it.

42
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,640
That's it?

43
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:13,120
So there's nothing left to do?

44
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,400
You don't need to do anything else.

45
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,800
I'll handle the rest.

46
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,280
Your payment, as agreed.

47
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,160
Thank you.

48
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,920
Then,

49
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,320
I…

50
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:07,080
I will finish the report and send it over.

51
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:10,000
Should I send it to the office
or your house?

52
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,200
Email it.

53
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,000
No need to come in person.
It's a waste of time.

54
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,160
Okay.

55
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:24,480
I'll email it

56
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,640
once it's done.

57
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,200
I'm going now.

58
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,840
Thank you

59
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,840
for giving me this job.

60
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:24,040
It was a really new experience.

61
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,520
But it was fun.

62
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,760
And thank you

63
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,800
for trusting me to work with you.

64
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,480
Goodbye.

65
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,920
<i>About Cent,</i>

66
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:39,040
<i>you were wrong, Yuan.</i>

67
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,680
<i>End of job, we split ways.</i>

68
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,640
Fuang!

69
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,400
Fuang!

70
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,520
Fuang.

71
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,840
Yes?

72
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:57,200
Can you stay another day and help?

73
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,040
Huh?

74
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,520
The work I need help with

75
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,280
is contacting the participants

76
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:07,360
and acting as the host,

77
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,280
moderating the conversation in my place.

78
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,120
Huh?

79
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,320
Me?

80
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,600
Yes.

81
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,040
Will you do it?

82
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,440
<i>He doesn't even have to ask.</i>

83
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,120
You're obviously going to say yes.

84
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:28,520
At first, I was unsure
because I've never done this before.

85
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,000
But then I thought,

86
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:33,520
anything that pays, I'll do it.

87
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,200
Right now, money matters the most.

88
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,480
True.

89
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:40,920
But honestly, Cent
has been really generous with you.

90
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,280
And the other day at my house,

91
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,920
he was less strict.

92
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,960
Even when Pound threw up on him,
he didn't say a single word.

93
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,960
He's like a different person now.

94
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,320
Did you

95
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,040
put a spell on him or what?

96
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:55,200
What spell?

97
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,280
I'm just working hard.

98
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:00,720
From what I've seen
while working with him,

99
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,240
he's a total workaholic.

100
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,760
He barely sleeps because of work.

101
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:11,160
I probably did the work the way
he likes, so now he's less strict.

102
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:14,600
And I think someone like him

103
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,760
probably doesn't think
about anything except work.

104
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,800
"What if I do think about it?

105
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:22,400
Would you feel the same way I do, Fuang?"

106
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,520
Oh, come on!

107
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,040
Whoa, Fuang!

108
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,240
Serves you right.

109
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,320
Ugh! I don't know.

110
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,920
As for me,

111
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:37,080
I'll let him think about it first,
then I'll decide

112
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,440
if I should think about it too.

113
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:40,880
Oh my God, you're too slow!

114
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:45,000
Be careful,
someone's gonna steal him first.

115
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,960
That must be Franc. I'll go open the door.

116
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,040
Hey, wait.

117
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:00,240
Did Franc ever ask you
anything about Cent?

118
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,600
A little.

119
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,520
She doesn't really want me
working with him.

120
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,600
Why do you ask?

121
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,640
Nothing. Just curious.

122
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,120
I don't like it. It's not pretty.

123
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,320
Then tell me what you don't like.

124
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,400
Say it.

125
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,040
I think it looks outdated.

126
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,520
The colors are too plain.

127
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:30,480
I want a more vibrant mood.

128
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:32,840
Something easy to remember.

129
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:36,400
And for the English lettering,
I changed my mind. I want Thai instead.

130
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,120
Bottom line,

131
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,640
it's just not wow enough.

132
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,320
Is it that bad?

133
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,080
Let me see.

134
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,160
I think it's cute, though.

135
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:53,160
It's a minimalist color palette.

136
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,880
And the font looks stylish.
I don't see anything outdated.

137
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,160
Thanks for your opinion,
but this is my work.

138
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,120
You've got to listen to my feedback.

139
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,160
When you designed for her,
I didn't say anything.

140
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,040
You're saying I'm butting in?

141
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:09,200
I didn't say that.
If you think so, I can't help it.

142
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,640
I think so.

143
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,280
Because you criticize
everyone in the world.

144
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:16,800
The only person you don't criticize
is yourself.

145
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:21,280
Hey, Bonus. If you have a problem with me,
don't take it out on my work.

146
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:24,960
You want to open a shop,
I want to start a YouTube channel.

147
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,640
I've invested a lot.
This logo is important to me.

148
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,920
If I don't like it,
I have the right to change it.

149
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,840
Because I'm not getting it for free.
I paid for it.

150
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,880
I know you're paying.

151
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:38,280
But this is about friendship.

152
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:42,680
Hiring a friend doesn't mean
you can talk down to them or say whatever.

153
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,840
Bonus, you're being dramatic.
Fuang hasn't even said anything.

154
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,600
She's not, so I have to speak for her.

155
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,600
You can't just stay quiet, can you?

156
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,360
You can't even be nice to your friend?

157
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,480
Stop!

158
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:55,480
What is wrong with you two?

159
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,120
Why are you even fighting?!

160
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,280
Bonus.

161
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,320
Thanks for caring.

162
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,640
I've dealt with clients
way harsher than this.

163
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,520
I'm fine.

164
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,440
And you,

165
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:16,200
I'll revise your work
based on your comments.

166
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,440
That's it.

167
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,120
This project is really important to me.

168
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,480
I want everything
to be perfect. You get it?

169
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,200
If my comments mean extra work for you,

170
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,640
just tell me how much extra
it costs. I'll pay.

171
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:38,880
And I don't think that just because I pay,
I can talk down to my friends.

172
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:44,480
For me, work is work, friends are friends.

173
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,160
Everyone should act professional at work.

174
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,480
Got it?

175
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,360
I'll go see her out.

176
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,280
Hey, Franc.

177
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,160
What's her problem with me?

178
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,720
She keeps snapping at me lately.

179
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,240
It's not even her business.

180
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,880
Come on, relax.

181
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:21,080
Try to understand. She's stressed about
opening her shop, so she's irritated.

182
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:27,040
Don't worry about your work. I'll fix it.

183
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,200
Yeah.

184
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,160
About Cent's comments on my work,

185
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:36,800
he was right about a lot of things.

186
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,640
I'll try to trust you on this.

187
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,360
I'll keep an open mind
and not let my emotions take over.

188
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:46,960
Maybe his harsh comments
can actually help with my work.

189
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,840
Anyway, next time

190
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:55,080
you work with him, can I come too?
I want to get to know him better.

191
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:58,720
Get to know him better?

192
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,840
Yeah, what you told me.

193
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:05,000
If I got to know him like you do,
I'd realize he isn't as bad as I thought.

194
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,760
I actually believe you now.

195
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,400
So I just want to see for myself.

196
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:12,240
Maybe if I get to know him more,

197
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,720
I might not even hate him anymore. Right?

198
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:20,160
I'm going now.
I'll leave the revisions to you.

199
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,880
I knew it. She's interested in Cent.

200
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,680
Why do you think so?

201
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:43,040
Because she's always interested
in anyone you're interested in.

202
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:48,400
I don't want to make you feel bad, okay,

203
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,320
but it's been like this
since we were kids.

204
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:52,040
Whenever you get close to someone,

205
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,280
she forces herself into that circle.

206
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,200
And when you start getting attention,

207
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,440
she inserts herself

208
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,320
and takes that attention away from you.

209
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,360
When we were kids,
I didn't think much of it,

210
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:09,080
but as we grew up, it got worse.

211
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:12,160
I can't stand it anymore,
especially with Peace.

212
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,560
What does he have to do with this?

213
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,400
You never said a thing,

214
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,040
but everyone in the group knew

215
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,920
you and Peace were a thing.

216
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,800
The whole group?

217
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:26,000
Well, Peace had his eye on you
since grade 11, right?

218
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:28,600
But in the end, you just hesitated,

219
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,240
and Franc ended up stepping in.

220
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,840
I really don't like it

221
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:36,920
that she said
she didn't even know you liked Peace.

222
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:40,000
Honestly, I don't believe her.

223
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:46,320
I'm not saying this
to make you feel bad or overthink it.

224
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,840
I just want to warn you.

225
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:51,960
If one day you and Cent
ever think about going beyond work

226
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,680
and want a relationship,

227
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,840
I think you should
watch out for her a bit.

228
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,720
Oh, Pound's calling.

229
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,040
Hello.

230
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:11,400
What's up, Bonus? I saw your missed call.

231
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:14,359
I remember you have the IC exam today,

232
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:16,440
so I just wanted to call
and wish you luck.

233
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:20,160
Good luck passing. Get a great score!

234
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:22,800
Yeah. Thanks, Bonus.

235
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,319
Hey, Fuang is here too.

236
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,319
Fuang, wish him luck.
He's got an exam today.

237
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:30,280
Good luck, buddy.

238
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,560
Hope you pass. Sadhu!

239
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:35,520
Yeah, sadhu.

240
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:39,320
Hey, will you get your result
right after the exam?

241
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:40,840
Yeah, I'll know by this evening.

242
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,680
Nice. Let me know, okay?

243
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:46,960
My parents are rooting for you too.

244
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:49,440
They even want to treat you to a meal.

245
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,280
Actually, just come eat at my house.

246
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:54,680
My mom will cook your favorite.

247
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,280
-Just text me when you know.
-Of course.

248
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,360
I'm gonna pass for sure.

249
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,240
Tell your parents
to prepare a big meal, okay?

250
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,120
You can do it. Good luck.

251
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,040
Keep me updated. Bye.

252
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,960
Let's go, Pound.

253
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:20,920
What?

254
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:27,600
Nothing. I was just worried about him.

255
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,840
How is he now?

256
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,400
Any updates on his situation?

257
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,600
He's getting better.
He'll move on eventually.

258
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:44,400
If anything comes up, I'll update you.

259
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,960
You better update me on everything,
not just work.

260
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,720
Update your status too.

261
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,120
-Huh?
-Yeah.

262
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,120
What does that mean?

263
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,400
Fuang, what do you mean?

264
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:04,400
Don't forget. Update your status too.

265
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:06,320
I'm off. Bye.

266
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,400
What do you mean by status, Fuang?

267
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:12,200
Hey, I don't get it.

268
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:13,840
What are you saying?

269
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:22,280
Good luck, everyone. You may begin.

270
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,760
Time's up.

271
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,120
You may check your results now.

272
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,080
Yes!

273
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:07,320
Congrats, man.

274
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:09,600
What time do you get off today?
Let's celebrate.

275
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,800
Not today.

276
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,480
I'm skipping work
to go learn pattern-making.

277
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,960
If I sign up, I have to start immediately.

278
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,920
I'll be done late. Let's do it next time.

279
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,240
Okay. Good luck.

280
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,360
Yeah. That's it for now.

281
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,440
Good luck. Congrats again.

282
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:28,080
Yeah, see you.

283
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,640
Taking leave again?

284
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,880
Where are you going?

285
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,760
Be careful with it.

286
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:46,680
Bonus is about to open a cake shop,
so I'm going to help her out.

287
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:52,400
Is that so?
Where is it? When's the opening?

288
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,120
At the mall near her house.
It opens next month.

289
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:59,960
Alright. Tell her
I'll drop by and support her.

290
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,000
Okay.

291
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:06,680
Hey, Yong.

292
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:07,880
Huh?

293
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:10,440
I'll make up for the hours later.

294
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:11,920
I'll do overtime. No OT pay needed.

295
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,120
Okay, good.

296
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,360
I'll let Uncle know.

297
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:16,960
Yes.

298
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,120
Hey, try not to take leave so often.

299
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,320
Yes.

300
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,680
The basic pattern class is already full.

301
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,360
We don't know when it will open again.

302
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,320
Please check our Facebook page.

303
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,560
Can't you add one more person?

304
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:38,000
Sorry, we can't.
One class only takes six students.

305
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:40,400
If we add more, it won't be manageable.

306
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,120
You can give my reserved spot to him.

307
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,480
You're not taking the class, Mr. Guy?

308
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:46,120
I already took the basic course once.

309
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,760
I'll just wait for Level Two.

310
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:51,840
He seems really determined,
so I'd rather give him my spot.

311
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,960
Thank you so much.

312
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:58,240
Hey, you don't have to bow.

313
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:01,000
Just focus on your studies.

314
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:04,920
Please put his name in place of mine.

315
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:08,400
No need to refund the payment.
Just carry it over to Level Two.

316
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,800
Actually, I'd like both of you to study.

317
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:13,320
Let me ask Teacher Pat if we can do that.

318
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,560
Sure.

319
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:20,800
Welcome to the men's clothing
pattern-making class, everyone.

320
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:28,960
Before we start the lesson,
let's get familiar with today's tools.

321
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,560
Show me your tools.

322
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:33,400
Place them in front of you.

323
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,360
Oh, nice.

324
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,840
What tools are you using?

325
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,720
Let me take a look.

326
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:49,640
Here. You can borrow mine.

327
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:53,000
It's okay, Guy.

328
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:55,680
Just take it. You don't have any, right?

329
00:23:01,320 --> 00:23:02,360
Thank you, Guy.

330
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:04,960
You've helped me twice already.

331
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:06,880
If you need anything, just tell me.

332
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:09,800
Yeah, I will.

333
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,320
Yes.

334
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,680
Focus on the class.

335
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:13,920
Yes.

336
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:21,040
You really can't come, right?

337
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:25,520
It's okay, Auntie. Thank you so much.

338
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:38,160
Only four people can make it.

339
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:41,040
But Cent needs five or six.

340
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:44,880
Mom!

341
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:47,240
Mom!

342
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:50,800
-Mom!
-What? Why are you shouting like that?

343
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,960
Can you help me with Cent's work?

344
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,840
What kind of work?

345
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:56,840
It's easy, Mom.

346
00:23:56,920 --> 00:24:01,920
Just sit, chat, and discuss work problems.
You get paid 3,000 baht.

347
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,120
I still can't find enough people for him.

348
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:08,480
Mom, please help me out.

349
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:10,720
I can help you.

350
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:13,360
But will Cent be okay with it, dear?

351
00:24:16,240 --> 00:24:17,160
<i>No problem.</i>

352
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:19,160
Aunt Pim probably
has some interesting insights.

353
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:21,960
<i>So now we've got everyone, including Mom,</i>

354
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:23,560
Lemon, who sells second-hand bags,

355
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:26,600
Aunt Ped, who sells chili paste,
Suchart the motorbike rider,

356
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,360
and Uncle Jod
from the appliance repair shop.

357
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,800
You met him when you fixed
the company's system. Remember?

358
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:32,720
<i>No.</i>

359
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:36,880
<i>But I'm okay with all of them.</i>

360
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,120
I trust you.

361
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,200
Thank you for trusting me.

362
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:44,920
SOM TAM PALACE

363
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,680
Let's hope nothing goes wrong.

364
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:50,760
Hey. Things were going so well,
and now you're stressing me out.

365
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:56,200
But okay. I'll do my best, Boss.

366
00:24:58,000 --> 00:24:59,040
Good.

367
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:02,720
-See you tomorrow.
-Okay. See you.

368
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:12,040
Are you okay, Mom? You look pale.

369
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,440
Lost your appetite?

370
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,560
Maybe I didn't sleep well.

371
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:20,000
You're eating so little.

372
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:26,360
You've started noticing
the people around you now.

373
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:29,480
Must've learned that from Fuang, huh?

374
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,040
What?

375
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,920
No. I've always been observant.

376
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,000
But you never used to notice me.

377
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:45,120
Back when we used to eat together,

378
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:47,520
you just ate with your head down.

379
00:25:47,600 --> 00:25:49,760
Then you'd go straight back
to your computer.

380
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:53,240
You never cared how much I ate

381
00:25:53,320 --> 00:25:57,520
and what I liked or didn't like.
Now you're starting to notice people.

382
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:01,320
How's working with Fuang?

383
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,760
It's…

384
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,880
-It's fine.
-Fine?

385
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:10,240
That's it?

386
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:11,760
At least I don't scold her.

387
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:15,720
Fair enough.

388
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:18,400
Pim will help you tomorrow. I'll go too.

389
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,440
-Why?
-I'm the investor.

390
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:24,920
I want to see

391
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,440
how things are going with Fuang.

392
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:30,080
I want to see
what you meant by "it's fine".

393
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:33,880
Oh.

394
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,360
I'll go late in the morning.

395
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:38,120
-Pong will come with me.
-Whatever.

396
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:40,920
I'm done eating.

397
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:42,880
Huh?

398
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:45,640
Mom!

399
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:48,520
Just a cramp.

400
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:50,440
-Sit down. I'll massage it for you.
-Wait.

401
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,600
I'm fine now.

402
00:26:56,760 --> 00:26:57,920
I'll join later.

403
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:01,160
Late morning. Don't worry.

404
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:10,880
When you do the interview,
I'll be in that room.

405
00:27:16,880 --> 00:27:18,480
I'll be observing from there.

406
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:20,880
The cameras will also be set up inside.

407
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:24,360
Besides the focus group we invited,

408
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,360
there will be an expert observing too.

409
00:27:26,440 --> 00:27:27,720
His name is Mr. Art.

410
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:33,240
Nervous?

411
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:36,440
Yes.

412
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:40,320
If you are nervous,

413
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:41,960
count from one to ten.

414
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:44,960
Breathe in and out slowly.

415
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:46,640
Stay calm.

416
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:49,120
Focus on the present. Don't worry.

417
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:51,320
Try it.

418
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,600
KWANSRI, PIM, SUCHART, LEMON, JOD, ART

419
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:08,200
If you're ready,

420
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,760
let's begin.

421
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,600
Everyone wants to be rich,

422
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:22,160
have jobs, make money,
and increase their income.

423
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:25,400
So we invited everyone here today to talk

424
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:28,320
and come up with a new service

425
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,200
in the form of an application

426
00:28:30,280 --> 00:28:32,520
to solve everyone's problems.

427
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:35,440
My only problem is my debt.

428
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:37,480
No matter how much I earn,
I can't pay it off.

429
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:38,920
Can you give me a loan?

430
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:42,520
Hey, kid. You got 200,000 baht?

431
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:43,760
Huh?

432
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:47,760
Our service doesn't help with debt.

433
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:50,960
It's to help increase income.

434
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:54,120
Aunt Ped, you might have
to work a bit more. But--

435
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:57,080
You said the app would reduce my trips.

436
00:28:57,160 --> 00:28:59,520
Now you're saying more work?

437
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,560
About motorbike taxis…

438
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:03,960
I'm a second-hand designer bag seller.

439
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:08,320
When I call a motorbike taxi,
sometimes it costs 100, sometimes 60.

440
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:10,160
Why isn't there a standard price?

441
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:12,560
Traffic isn't the same all day.

442
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:14,800
At lunchtime and after work,

443
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,560
it's much heavier,

444
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:19,240
so it takes longer.

445
00:29:19,320 --> 00:29:22,720
But if you charge this much,
customers won't order from me.

446
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:25,680
Then I can't sell my bags,
and you don't get rides either.

447
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:28,080
Can't you lower it a bit?

448
00:29:28,160 --> 00:29:29,160
No, sis.

449
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:31,280
Fuel prices keep going up every day.

450
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:32,880
I'm barely getting by as it is.

451
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:37,200
Then Lemon and Suchart can meet halfway.

452
00:29:38,040 --> 00:29:41,600
Then Lemon and Suchart can meet halfway.

453
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,200
Lemon pays the ride fare for customers,

454
00:29:44,280 --> 00:29:48,000
and Suchart lowers the price
during peak hours.

455
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:51,960
Both of you will make a little less profit

456
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:54,440
but earn a more consistent income.

457
00:29:54,520 --> 00:29:57,160
That way, everyone benefits equally.

458
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:58,880
It's a win-win for both sides.

459
00:29:58,960 --> 00:30:02,160
Your customers aren't affected either.

460
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:04,960
Is this a good solution?

461
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:07,320
If the jobs are consistent

462
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:09,960
and not too far, it's actually doable.

463
00:30:10,560 --> 00:30:13,640
If the fare doesn't get so expensive
that customers run away,

464
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:17,400
I'm okay with it.
I can take a small hit on my profit.

465
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:25,000
<i>Hey, kid, I'm an appliance repairman.</i>

466
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:27,200
<i>So what would I even sell on this app?</i>

467
00:30:27,280 --> 00:30:30,760
<i>For you, Uncle Jod, it's service-based.</i>

468
00:30:30,840 --> 00:30:34,280
If customers are interested,
they can book your repair service.

469
00:30:34,360 --> 00:30:37,240
But I'm not good with this stuff.
I can't really use apps.

470
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:39,840
Here's the thing, kid.
Can't you just tell me what to do

471
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:42,200
without making me click anything?

472
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,400
Then could Suchart help?

473
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:47,400
If a customer requests his repair service,

474
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:49,600
Suchart could receive the request
and notify him.

475
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:51,560
Once you accept the job,

476
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:55,200
Suchart confirms it in the app
and picks up the item from the customer.

477
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:56,720
<i>After you finish repairing it,</i>

478
00:30:56,800 --> 00:31:00,160
<i>Suchart delivers it back to the customer.</i>

479
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:04,000
<i>So both he and you will earn more income.</i>

480
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:07,160
It works like a commission system.
Is that okay?

481
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:09,000
<i>If there are more customers on the app,</i>

482
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,320
<i>I'll earn more too.</i>

483
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,080
<i>May I ask something?</i>

484
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,320
<i>From what I've heard,</i>

485
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:17,680
I don't really see how your service
is different from others out there.

486
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:21,480
What makes yours better?
Why should I use it?

487
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:24,040
If you can't answer that,

488
00:31:24,120 --> 00:31:26,000
I don't think your app will make it.

489
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:30,320
Our app is different
because we use a pre-order system.

490
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:34,200
Partner stores will receive
clear daily orders.

491
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:37,840
Sellers can stock up in advance
without taking extra orders daily.

492
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:40,600
This increases their income
and gives them more free time to rest

493
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,720
or sell through other channels.

494
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:44,680
Most importantly,

495
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:49,080
we charge lower GP than others,
or none at all.

496
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:50,840
You're willing to run at a loss?

497
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:54,000
The goal of the app
isn't to make a profit.

498
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:57,480
It's to help improve small businesses,

499
00:31:57,560 --> 00:31:59,480
expand their sales channels,

500
00:31:59,560 --> 00:32:02,320
and increase income
for daily wage workers.

501
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:06,680
Our app connects everyone who uses it
into one system,

502
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,920
not just buyers with sellers,

503
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,120
but sellers with other sellers too.

504
00:32:11,920 --> 00:32:13,400
This application

505
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:15,520
helps everyone move forward together

506
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:18,040
and improves their quality of life
through technology.

507
00:32:18,120 --> 00:32:21,160
All of this is the vision of my mother,

508
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:23,760
who funded the development of this app.

509
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:41,240
Thank you so much for coming today, Pim.

510
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:43,040
It's really nothing, Eiang.

511
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:45,920
I just sat and listened.
I didn't do anything.

512
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:47,040
That's already tiring.

513
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:51,800
Today, you look a bit tired.

514
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,800
I probably didn't sleep much last night.

515
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,360
-I stayed up late. I was excited.
-Yes.

516
00:33:00,440 --> 00:33:01,440
I was just excited.

517
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:05,440
Oh, your hair.

518
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:07,440
-Sorry, let me get that for you.
-It's okay, I'll do it.

519
00:33:11,080 --> 00:33:14,640
I told you to stop changing shampoos
based on reviews.

520
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:17,280
Every time she sees a new one,

521
00:33:17,360 --> 00:33:19,520
she just keeps buying and trying it.

522
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:20,840
When she gets an allergy,

523
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:23,080
her hair starts falling out
in clumps like this.

524
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,400
I see.

525
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:28,120
Yes, I know. You talk too much.

526
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:31,320
It'll get better once I stop using it.

527
00:33:32,480 --> 00:33:34,080
-This is Pong.
-Yes.

528
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:37,080
She's my assistant.
She's been with me for years.

529
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,000
Oh.

530
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:40,360
-I even opened a som tam shop for her.
-Right.

531
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,880
The one I gave you to try at home.

532
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,000
I see.

533
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,760
I'll invite you to eat at the shop.

534
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:47,560
-Sure, Eiang.
-Hello.

535
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:49,880
-Hello. It was really delicious.
-Thank you so much.

536
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:52,920
I've heard a lot about you and Fuang.

537
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:54,240
I'm glad to finally meet you.

538
00:33:54,320 --> 00:33:56,560
Please come visit my shop sometime.

539
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:57,880
I'll take good care of you.

540
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:59,240
Thank you.

541
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:00,440
My pleasure.

542
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:04,480
I think I should head back now.
Traffic might get bad.

543
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:05,520
Come eat at my place sometime.

544
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,120
-Okay?
-Yes.

545
00:34:07,200 --> 00:34:08,440
-Goodbye, Eiang.
-Let's go.

546
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,360
Goodbye.

547
00:34:11,080 --> 00:34:12,560
-Traffic's getting bad.
-Okay.

548
00:34:17,679 --> 00:34:19,639
Your app idea is good,

549
00:34:19,719 --> 00:34:23,800
though it's a bit unrealistic
to build non-profit app.

550
00:34:23,880 --> 00:34:25,840
Does your mother really think that way?

551
00:34:26,440 --> 00:34:29,880
-Yes.
-Wow. Noble intention.

552
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:30,920
I'm rooting for you.

553
00:34:31,520 --> 00:34:33,960
By the way, I recently spoke with Kenji.

554
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:36,120
I heard Pay-Wai is launching in Thailand?

555
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:39,320
We're considering it.
Probably after the app is more developed.

556
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:41,719
With your skills, it shouldn't take long.

557
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:44,320
But why don't you hire
younger people for this?

558
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:47,600
Anyway, I'll take my leave now.

559
00:34:47,679 --> 00:34:50,639
Just one thing.
Your assistant is really good.

560
00:34:50,719 --> 00:34:52,639
She looks good,
has potential, and is talented.

561
00:34:52,719 --> 00:34:54,719
Young talent is rare these days.

562
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:57,680
Take good care of her. I'm heading off.

563
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:25,080
Thirty thousand?

564
00:35:30,560 --> 00:35:31,800
Thanks for helping out.

565
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:35,520
But…

566
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:37,920
Isn't this too much?

567
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,400
I didn't really do much.

568
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:42,640
-Don't want it?
-I do!

569
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:45,880
Thank you.

570
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:51,520
After being forced to do work
you didn't want to do,

571
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:53,920
now you can go back
to what you actually want to do.

572
00:35:54,720 --> 00:35:58,360
No, it's not like that.
Helping you didn't feel forced.

573
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:01,520
Even though it was difficult,

574
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,240
and I'd never done it before,

575
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:06,120
I learned a lot, including today.

576
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:19,680
You said you needed help with work
for one more day,

577
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:25,280
and today's job is done.

578
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:28,440
That means

579
00:36:29,160 --> 00:36:32,080
I'm done here, right?

580
00:36:36,560 --> 00:36:37,640
You're done.

581
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:52,040
Okay.

582
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,440
-Well…
-Well…

583
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:08,200
Then,

584
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:09,440
I…

585
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:13,880
I'll get going.

586
00:37:32,680 --> 00:37:33,920
Fuang.

587
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:36,440
Yes?

588
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:44,880
Focus on your own work.

589
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,600
Don't spend all your time helping others.

590
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:55,080
Got it?

591
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:07,160
Yes.

592
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:13,840
Then…

593
00:38:16,080 --> 00:38:17,120
I'm leaving.

594
00:38:58,080 --> 00:38:59,360
Mom.

595
00:39:00,520 --> 00:39:03,680
You just walked right past me.
Didn't you see?

596
00:39:04,920 --> 00:39:05,880
I didn't.

597
00:39:06,880 --> 00:39:07,960
You were spacing out, huh?

598
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:10,320
Let's hurry and go home.
Your dad's waiting for dinner.

599
00:39:13,760 --> 00:39:16,520
Oh! Sorry, please wait.

600
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:17,800
Let's go.

601
00:39:17,880 --> 00:39:19,240
Can we get on too?

602
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:29,720
Fuang! Come on, dear.

603
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:32,320
-They're waiting.
-Yes.

604
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:33,720
Sorry.

605
00:39:35,120 --> 00:39:36,680
Nick!

606
00:39:40,640 --> 00:39:42,040
What are you doing?

607
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:44,880
I'm checking the plumbing.
The water isn't flowing.

608
00:39:44,960 --> 00:39:46,240
Huh?

609
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:54,800
Hey.

610
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:57,000
What do we do now, Nick?

611
00:39:59,240 --> 00:40:01,880
I don't think the pump is broken,

612
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:06,360
but we'll need to call a plumber.
That's all I can figure out for now.

613
00:40:06,440 --> 00:40:07,760
Really?

614
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:10,520
How much will it cost?

615
00:40:12,560 --> 00:40:14,960
We'll have to let the plumber check first.

616
00:40:15,040 --> 00:40:19,040
If it's not broken, maybe under 10,000.

617
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:21,600
But if it is,

618
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:24,240
it could be

619
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:27,880
30,000 to 40,000
for a good replacement pump.

620
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,800
Thirty thousand to 40,000 baht?

621
00:40:32,520 --> 00:40:34,200
Where are we going to get the money?

622
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:35,320
I'll pay for it.

623
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:42,400
Cent just transferred my payment,
about 50,000 total.

624
00:40:42,480 --> 00:40:44,160
I'll send 40,000 for the pump.

625
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:46,480
-Well…
-No, Fuang.

626
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:49,320
You should keep that money for yourself.

627
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:52,440
Yeah, that's your first salary.

628
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:54,480
We'll sort out the money

629
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:57,400
-from another source. Don't worry.
-Yes.

630
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:59,840
It's fine, Dad. Please take it.

631
00:41:02,200 --> 00:41:04,320
The graphic design work
I uploaded on the website

632
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:08,000
has got a lot of clients contacting me.
It's not a problem.

633
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,040
Thank you, dear.

634
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:32,600
Thank you, dear.

635
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:36,600
NOT APPROVED, NO MAIL

636
00:41:37,240 --> 00:41:39,480
No new work.
Even the sticker designs got rejected.

637
00:41:46,120 --> 00:41:48,360
Working from home like this,

638
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:50,560
I can probably survive another month.

639
00:42:15,480 --> 00:42:17,320
FULLY THOUGHT-OUT CONCEPT, SOLID STORY

640
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:20,360
UNISEX APPEAL, NO VIOLENCE
EASY TO REMEMBER, A CLEAR UNIQUE DNA

641
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:22,960
Wow, you look
like you didn't sleep at all.

642
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:25,000
Working on graphic designs for clients?

643
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,720
-Yes.
-Huh?

644
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,840
Wash this for me.
I'll go check on the plumber.

645
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:32,640
Wait, Dad. What are you reading?

646
00:43:34,920 --> 00:43:36,320
It's about Gen Me.

647
00:43:37,040 --> 00:43:39,680
After I talked with Cent the other day,

648
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:43,600
I realized there are younger people
who actually understand me.

649
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:47,320
If I'm going back to editing work,
I think this book

650
00:43:47,400 --> 00:43:51,000
might help me communicate better.

651
00:43:51,080 --> 00:43:52,920
Gen Me is my generation.

652
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:54,760
What does it say?

653
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:57,520
Anything about money, work, love?

654
00:43:57,600 --> 00:44:00,240
Hey, it's not a fortune-telling book.

655
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:03,840
It says Gen Me grew up with technology.

656
00:44:05,400 --> 00:44:06,400
How so?

657
00:44:06,480 --> 00:44:08,200
Kind of like,

658
00:44:08,280 --> 00:44:11,240
they prefer working to live
rather than living to work.

659
00:44:11,320 --> 00:44:13,880
Not stuck in old rules.

660
00:44:13,960 --> 00:44:16,600
They're expressive.
They just do what they think.

661
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:20,840
They prefer being in communities
with like-minded people.

662
00:44:20,920 --> 00:44:22,320
Friends come first.

663
00:44:22,400 --> 00:44:24,000
Hey, that's totally me.

664
00:44:24,080 --> 00:44:27,600
Oh. And it also says,
if one is born into a big family,

665
00:44:27,680 --> 00:44:30,280
they're usually spoiled
by members of Gen X

666
00:44:30,360 --> 00:44:32,920
and Baby Boomers who are older.

667
00:44:33,480 --> 00:44:35,240
Basically very spoiled.

668
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:37,760
It's like Generation <i>Mee Bun</i>, so blessed.

669
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:38,800
Yeah.

670
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:45,120
<i>Mee Bun.</i>

671
00:44:47,920 --> 00:44:49,080
FULLY THOUGHT-OUT CONCEPT, SOLID STORY

672
00:45:32,040 --> 00:45:34,560
Is this Mee-Bun,
your first original character design?

673
00:45:34,640 --> 00:45:38,600
Yes, Mee-Bun. It represents Gen Me.

674
00:45:38,680 --> 00:45:41,440
It's independent, expressive, brave,

675
00:45:41,520 --> 00:45:42,840
friendly with technology,

676
00:45:42,920 --> 00:45:44,800
and cares about the environment.

677
00:45:44,880 --> 00:45:47,840
Mee-Bun is also a pun on bun,
inspired by her messy hair bun,

678
00:45:47,920 --> 00:45:50,480
like the hairstyle I like to wear.

679
00:45:52,960 --> 00:45:54,040
That's basically you.

680
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:56,800
It's cute. I like it.

681
00:45:56,880 --> 00:45:58,840
Even if others don't, I do.

682
00:45:58,920 --> 00:46:00,440
-Really?
-Yeah.

683
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:03,360
What will you do with it?

684
00:46:03,960 --> 00:46:07,000
I'm going to pitch Mee-Bun
to Cent and Aunt Eiang.

685
00:46:07,080 --> 00:46:09,360
If they're interested, I'll start planning

686
00:46:09,440 --> 00:46:11,800
the marketing and turn it into a product.

687
00:46:11,880 --> 00:46:15,360
But I want to start small.
I don't want to take too much from them.

688
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:16,920
-That sounds good.
-Yeah.

689
00:46:18,960 --> 00:46:19,920
By the way,

690
00:46:20,480 --> 00:46:22,000
about you and Cent,

691
00:46:22,880 --> 00:46:25,440
when you told me I was wrong,
what did you mean?

692
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:30,920
About you saying he likes me,

693
00:46:32,400 --> 00:46:34,560
it's nothing like that.

694
00:46:35,800 --> 00:46:37,240
After work, we go our separate ways.

695
00:46:37,320 --> 00:46:38,560
You were wrong.

696
00:46:38,640 --> 00:46:40,720
Then what about this?

697
00:46:41,360 --> 00:46:44,240
Mee-Bun, your first child.
Isn't it also his?

698
00:46:45,240 --> 00:46:49,560
No! This is my character, my work.
Aunt Eiang is the investor.

699
00:46:49,640 --> 00:46:51,000
It has nothing to do with Cent.

700
00:46:53,200 --> 00:46:54,680
I'm gonna ask you seriously.

701
00:46:54,760 --> 00:46:55,720
Yes.

702
00:46:55,800 --> 00:46:57,040
Do you like Cent?

703
00:47:00,720 --> 00:47:04,520
If you wait for him to make the first move
before showing how you feel,

704
00:47:05,120 --> 00:47:08,360
maybe love won't wait for you
the way you're waiting for it.

705
00:47:24,080 --> 00:47:25,240
Here you go.

706
00:47:26,480 --> 00:47:29,120
This is a dining table, not a work desk!

707
00:47:39,920 --> 00:47:41,760
He's not working
on the dining table anymore.

708
00:47:41,840 --> 00:47:44,920
He's working on a chair instead.
Case closed, Mom.

709
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:48,600
Other families tell their kids not to use
their phones at the dining table,

710
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:52,440
but in this house, I have to ban my son
from working at the dining table.

711
00:47:52,520 --> 00:47:54,600
It's called multitasking.
Super productive.

712
00:47:54,680 --> 00:47:55,920
I'm going to kick you.

713
00:47:57,120 --> 00:47:58,800
Please calm down. Let's eat first.

714
00:48:02,320 --> 00:48:04,720
The client is in a hurry,
so I have to rush. You get it?

715
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:05,960
I don't.

716
00:48:09,880 --> 00:48:11,800
<i>I mean, I get it, though.</i>

717
00:48:13,280 --> 00:48:14,600
But…

718
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:18,120
It's not that easy.

719
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:21,120
What about you? I've told you for ages.

720
00:48:21,200 --> 00:48:23,480
You still haven't had the courage
to tell Franc.

721
00:48:25,080 --> 00:48:26,360
Yeah.

722
00:48:26,440 --> 00:48:28,040
You're right.

723
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:32,240
Honestly, we might just be the type
who are good at talking,

724
00:48:32,320 --> 00:48:33,600
but scared of doing it.

725
00:48:35,800 --> 00:48:37,160
True.

726
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:43,360
Wait.

727
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:46,120
If you agree with me like that,

728
00:48:46,200 --> 00:48:47,880
are you admitting you like Cent?

729
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:52,240
See?

730
00:48:52,760 --> 00:48:54,440
You just admitted it.

731
00:48:54,520 --> 00:48:57,520
No wonder you keep talking
about Cent all the time.

732
00:48:57,600 --> 00:48:59,080
You always mention him.

733
00:48:59,160 --> 00:49:00,680
You're totally falling for him.

734
00:49:00,760 --> 00:49:03,720
Wait, no. It's just…

735
00:49:03,800 --> 00:49:06,160
a good feeling, like a feel-good vibe.

736
00:49:06,240 --> 00:49:08,480
A good feeling, like a feel-good vibe?

737
00:49:08,560 --> 00:49:09,840
Yeah.

738
00:49:09,920 --> 00:49:11,400
Just say you like him.

739
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:16,280
But honestly, I'm rooting for you two.

740
00:49:20,760 --> 00:49:23,880
Just don't mess it up like you did
with Peace last time.

741
00:49:25,360 --> 00:49:27,040
When will you pitch it to him?

742
00:49:31,040 --> 00:49:32,440
I don't even know yet.

743
00:49:32,520 --> 00:49:35,120
Don't know? Then why don't you just ask?

744
00:49:35,840 --> 00:49:37,040
Well.

745
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:39,480
It's her job. She should
be the one following up,

746
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:41,280
not the investor chasing her.

747
00:49:43,600 --> 00:49:45,920
Fuang isn't some stranger.

748
00:49:46,000 --> 00:49:50,240
She's a good kid. Kind, helpful,
and she understands you best.

749
00:49:50,960 --> 00:49:53,160
See? You only gave her a little guidance,

750
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:56,160
and she can speak for you like she's you.

751
00:49:56,240 --> 00:49:58,360
People like that are rare.

752
00:50:00,280 --> 00:50:03,640
Even if you don't work together anymore,
you can still be friends.

753
00:50:04,440 --> 00:50:06,920
Is Kenji the only friend
you're going to have?

754
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:10,520
If he sells his shares
and moves on with his life,

755
00:50:10,600 --> 00:50:12,040
you'll have no one left.

756
00:50:16,160 --> 00:50:19,160
But anyway, Fuang is really sweet.

757
00:50:19,840 --> 00:50:22,040
Soon she'll be dating

758
00:50:22,120 --> 00:50:23,760
and building her own family.

759
00:50:24,320 --> 00:50:26,000
She won't care about you either.

760
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:30,800
<i>Take your medicine first.</i>

761
00:50:35,280 --> 00:50:38,680
By the way, you'd make a great barista.

762
00:50:39,960 --> 00:50:42,120
-Why?
-You're really good at stirring things up.

763
00:50:42,200 --> 00:50:44,160
Strong brew indeed.

764
00:50:45,200 --> 00:50:48,800
I wonder if Mr. Cent can still stay cool
and unfazed after all this.

765
00:50:51,240 --> 00:50:52,440
I wonder too.

766
00:50:56,360 --> 00:50:57,960
Alright.

767
00:50:58,040 --> 00:50:59,080
Here we are.

768
00:51:04,200 --> 00:51:05,760
-Thanks.
-Yeah.

769
00:51:05,840 --> 00:51:07,640
You bought me snacks when I was broke.

770
00:51:07,720 --> 00:51:09,320
And thanks for dropping me off.

771
00:51:10,640 --> 00:51:12,840
It's payday, so I'm feeling generous.

772
00:51:15,120 --> 00:51:16,960
Having a salary would be nice.

773
00:51:17,720 --> 00:51:20,480
At least money comes in every month.

774
00:51:27,520 --> 00:51:29,920
-Cent!
-I told you.

775
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:32,720
He can't disappear for long.
What does he say?

776
00:51:36,320 --> 00:51:37,520
Tell me what he said.

777
00:51:37,600 --> 00:51:41,080
"How's the character design going?

778
00:51:41,160 --> 00:51:44,560
Ready to pitch yet?
If you're ready, come over.

779
00:51:45,400 --> 00:51:46,240
Mom told me to ask."

780
00:51:47,920 --> 00:51:48,960
Classic excuse.

781
00:51:49,600 --> 00:51:52,200
-What do you mean?
-He wants to see you,

782
00:51:52,280 --> 00:51:54,080
but he's using work
and his mom as an excuse.

783
00:51:54,760 --> 00:51:55,920
-Really?
-Of course.

784
00:51:58,240 --> 00:51:59,800
Hey, but…

785
00:51:59,880 --> 00:52:02,040
what if he's not using
his mom as an excuse

786
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:05,240
and Aunt Eiang really just asked?
I don't want to imagine things.

787
00:52:05,320 --> 00:52:06,720
Fine, let's do it like this.

788
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:10,320
Just reply like you're ready
and go pitch it tomorrow.

789
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:11,920
-Okay.
-Go ahead.

790
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:13,640
Hey, wait.

791
00:52:13,720 --> 00:52:16,080
What am I even going to pitch?

792
00:52:16,160 --> 00:52:18,080
What? Your Mee-Bun, of course.

793
00:52:18,680 --> 00:52:21,040
Honestly, your brain is gone.

794
00:52:22,080 --> 00:52:24,560
Okay. Mee-Bun, ready to pitch.

795
00:52:33,440 --> 00:52:34,680
Not replying?

796
00:52:38,320 --> 00:52:41,320
"I'm ready to pitch."

797
00:52:45,040 --> 00:52:46,120
-MOM TOLD ME TO ASK
-I'M READY TO PITCH

798
00:52:47,320 --> 00:52:53,560
"Is tomorrow convenient for you?"

799
00:52:57,320 --> 00:52:59,240
OKAY

800
00:53:02,160 --> 00:53:03,360
Okay!

801
00:53:03,440 --> 00:53:04,280
-Okay.
-Okay!

802
00:53:05,720 --> 00:53:07,080
Wait.

803
00:53:07,160 --> 00:53:08,520
Why did he just say okay?

804
00:53:08,600 --> 00:53:10,040
Does that mean he wants to see me?

805
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:11,840
Let me see.

806
00:53:12,440 --> 00:53:16,880
He replied immediately
after you sent that.

807
00:53:17,480 --> 00:53:20,400
That means he was waiting
for your message.

808
00:53:21,320 --> 00:53:23,800
He looks calm,
but I think he's actually happy.

809
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:28,200
-Hey, just reply to him.
-Really?

810
00:53:28,280 --> 00:53:29,200
Yeah.

811
00:53:29,880 --> 00:53:30,880
Just confirm it quickly.

812
00:53:32,200 --> 00:53:33,560
Hurry up.

813
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:39,080
SEE YOU TOMORROW

814
00:53:50,840 --> 00:53:52,280
Mee-Bun…

815
00:53:52,840 --> 00:53:55,200
might even get you a boyfriend.
Perfect timing.

816
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:59,120
Don't mess it up, girl! I'm off.

817
00:54:00,960 --> 00:54:02,240
Oh.

818
00:54:34,120 --> 00:54:36,640
Okay, I like it. I'm buying it.

819
00:54:36,720 --> 00:54:37,760
Let's go with this.

820
00:54:41,280 --> 00:54:42,320
Are you sure?

821
00:54:42,400 --> 00:54:44,640
Of course. This is so me.

822
00:54:45,160 --> 00:54:46,520
How much for the design?

823
00:54:47,280 --> 00:54:49,320
-I won't charge you.
-Hey, no way.

824
00:54:49,400 --> 00:54:52,760
I told you I was hiring you,
and I made you revise it so many times.

825
00:54:53,440 --> 00:54:56,120
I didn't charge Bonus,
and I won't charge you.

826
00:54:57,160 --> 00:54:59,880
I know you're trying to save money.
Just keep it.

827
00:55:02,640 --> 00:55:03,800
Let's do this instead.

828
00:55:05,160 --> 00:55:08,120
Once your channel starts making
the money you want,

829
00:55:08,200 --> 00:55:11,160
then you can pay me. Deal?

830
00:55:12,320 --> 00:55:14,920
Thanks for understanding.

831
00:55:16,560 --> 00:55:18,480
Honestly, I'm a bit scared.

832
00:55:18,560 --> 00:55:21,800
Once I looked into running a channel,
I realized it's not easy.

833
00:55:21,880 --> 00:55:23,960
There are so many steps

834
00:55:24,040 --> 00:55:25,560
before I can actually make money.

835
00:55:27,600 --> 00:55:29,400
It'll be fine.

836
00:55:30,240 --> 00:55:33,320
But once the channel is up,
you can't earn anything at all?

837
00:55:34,080 --> 00:55:36,840
You can, if advertisers come.

838
00:55:37,480 --> 00:55:39,240
But I don't even know if they will.

839
00:55:41,320 --> 00:55:44,440
To be honest, I've been thinking
about what Cent said.

840
00:55:45,520 --> 00:55:47,480
A lot of it makes sense.

841
00:55:49,160 --> 00:55:52,000
I want to meet him again for advice.
Can you set it up for me?

842
00:55:54,440 --> 00:55:56,280
-Fuang!
-Huh?

843
00:55:56,360 --> 00:55:57,760
When will you meet Cent again?

844
00:55:58,840 --> 00:56:00,200
I don't know.

845
00:56:01,160 --> 00:56:02,200
Well.

846
00:56:02,840 --> 00:56:05,880
We already finished the project,
so I don't know when we'll meet again.

847
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:08,600
Oh. That's a shame.

848
00:56:11,760 --> 00:56:14,080
You're not coming with me
to the clothing review?

849
00:56:14,160 --> 00:56:17,480
I've set it up with Yuan. After work,
we're going to grab food. I'll treat you!

850
00:56:18,200 --> 00:56:20,040
Sorry, I can't.

851
00:56:20,560 --> 00:56:24,080
I already made plans with my mom.
You and Yuan go ahead.

852
00:56:28,720 --> 00:56:31,680
If you want to get rich fast,
I can help you find ways

853
00:56:31,760 --> 00:56:34,320
to make your money grow. Interested?

854
00:56:34,400 --> 00:56:35,880
Nonsense!

855
00:56:36,480 --> 00:56:38,800
There's no such thing
as getting rich without working.

856
00:56:39,880 --> 00:56:41,120
That kind of idea

857
00:56:41,200 --> 00:56:42,880
only exists to trick greedy people.

858
00:56:42,960 --> 00:56:45,360
It cares about the environment

859
00:56:45,440 --> 00:56:48,360
and is very determined. It has dreams,

860
00:56:48,440 --> 00:56:50,080
but doesn't stick to old ways of thinking.

861
00:56:50,160 --> 00:56:51,480
And it's quietly stubborn.

862
00:56:58,040 --> 00:56:59,880
<i>When will you meet Cent again?</i>

863
00:56:59,960 --> 00:57:04,200
<i>I don't know. We finished the project,</i>
<i>so I don't know when we'll meet again.</i>

864
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:51,800
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
